.TH "CSSTRANSFORMVALUE" "3JS" "September 17, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSTransformValue \- CSSTransformValue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSTransformValue\f[B]\f[R] interface of the CSS Typed
Object Model API represents \f[CR]transform\-list\f[R] values as used by
the CSS \f[CR]transform\f[R] property.
It is an iterable of \f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R] objects, each
representing a single \f[CR]transform\-function\f[R].
.PP
The items can be accessed and set by index
(\f[CR]transformValue[0]\f[R]), and as an iterable it can be used with a
\f[CR]for...of\f[R] loop or the spread syntax.
.SH CONSTRUCTOR
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue()\f[R]
Creates a new \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.length\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns the number of items in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.is2D\f[R] \f[I](read\-only)\f[R]
Returns a boolean indicating whether the transform is 2D or 3D.
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Also inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]CSSStyleValue\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.toMatrix()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[CR]DOMMatrix\f[R] object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.entries()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields
\f[CR][index, value]\f[R] pairs for each item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.forEach()\f[R]
Executes a provided function once for each item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.keys()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields the index of each
item in the object.
.TP
\f[B]CSSTransformValue.values()\f[R]
Returns a new \f[I]array iterator\f[R] that yields each item in the
object.
.SH DESCRIPTION
Each item in a \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] is a
\f[CR]CSSTransformComponent\f[R]\-derived object, such as a
\f[CR]CSSScale\f[R] or \f[CR]CSSTranslate\f[R], representing a single
transform function object.
.PP
The \f[CR]CSSTransformValue()\f[R] constructor throws a
\f[CR]TypeError\f[R] if given an empty array \(em a
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] always contains at least one component.
.PP
\f[CR]CSSTransformValue.is2D\f[R] is \f[CR]true\f[R] only if every
component\(cqs own \f[CR]is2D\f[R] is \f[CR]true\f[R]; if any component
is a 3D transform, the whole \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] is treated as
3D.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Creating, reading, and updating a \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R]
This example creates a \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R], then reads its
items via \f[CR]length\f[R], indexed access, and iteration, and finally
replaces one of the items by assigning to its index.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTransformValue([
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSTranslate(CSS.px(10), CSS.px(20)),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(2, 3),
]);

console.log(transform.length); \f[I]// 2\f[R]
console.log(transform[0].toString()); \f[I]// \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px)\(dq\f[R]

\f[B]for\f[R] (\f[B]const\f[R] component \f[B]of\f[R] transform) {
  console.log(component.toString());
}
\f[I]// \(dqtranslate(10px, 20px)\(dq\f[R]
\f[I]// \(dqscale(2, 3)\(dq\f[R]

transform[1] = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSScale(4, 5);
console.log(transform[1].toString()); \f[I]// \(dqscale(4, 5)\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SS Reading a transform from a computed style map
A \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] instance is returned when you read the
value of the \f[CR]transform\f[R] property from a
\f[CR]StylePropertyMapReadOnly\f[R].
This example reads the computed \f[CR]transform\f[R] of a button styled
with \f[CR]transform: scale(0.95)\f[R].
See the \f[CR]CSSTransformValue\f[R] with \f[CR]CSSScale\f[R] section of
the CSS Typed OM guide for more detail on this example.
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]button\f[R] id=\(dqbtn\(dq>Styled button</\f[B]button\f[R]>
.EE
.IP
.EX
btn {
  \f[B]display\f[R]: inline\-block;
  \f[B]transform\f[R]: scale(0.95);
}
.EE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] styleMap = document.getElementById(\(dqbtn\(dq).computedStyleMap();
\f[B]const\f[R] transform = styleMap.get(\(dqtransform\(dq);

console.log(transform); \f[I]// CSSTransformValue {0: CSSScale, length: 1, is2D: true}\f[R]
console.log(transform.length); \f[I]// 1\f[R]
console.log(transform[0].x); \f[I]// CSSUnitValue {value: 0.95, unit: \(dqnumber\(dq}\f[R]
console.log(transform.is2D); \f[I]// true\f[R]
.EE
